Traffic Manager: forget a removed vehicle's junction entrance

LocalizationStage keeps, for each vehicle at the entrance of a junction, the
junction's end point and a safe point after it (vehicles_at_junction_entrance,
handed on to the motion plan stage), but neither RemoveActor() nor Reset() cleared
it: it kept the SimpleWaypoints of removed vehicles alive after their
InMemoryMap was destroyed, and a later vehicle that reused the actor id got
the old junction's points. RemoveActor() now erases the vehicle's entry and
Reset() clears them all.

Applied by typesafe_carla's cmake/FetchCarla.cmake to the fetched LibCarla;
being proposed upstream (carla-simulator/carla). Drop this patch once every
ref in tools/release_carla_refs.txt has the fix.

diff --git a/LibCarla/source/carla/trafficmanager/LocalizationStage.cpp b/LibCarla/source/carla/trafficmanager/LocalizationStage.cpp
index 8fd7b17..075752a 100644
--- a/LibCarla/source/carla/trafficmanager/LocalizationStage.cpp
+++ b/LibCarla/source/carla/trafficmanager/LocalizationStage.cpp
@@ -438,3 +438,4 @@ void LocalizationStage::HandleLargeVehicleJunction(const ActorId actor_id,
 void LocalizationStage::RemoveActor(ActorId actor_id) {
     last_lane_change_swpt.erase(actor_id);
+    vehicles_at_junction_entrance.erase(actor_id);
     vehicles_at_junction.erase(actor_id);
@@ -445,3 +446,4 @@ void LocalizationStage::RemoveActor(ActorId actor_id) {
 void LocalizationStage::Reset() {
   last_lane_change_swpt.clear();
+  vehicles_at_junction_entrance.clear();
   vehicles_at_junction.clear();
